{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "sanitized-baseline.schema.json",
  "title": "TASK-025 sanitized baseline",
  "$comment": "Canonical JSON: UTF-8 without BOM, LF line endings, sorted object keys, two-space indentation, exactly one trailing LF. Timestamps are UTC ISO-8601 with Z and millisecond precision. Arrays use REQ-009 stable sort keys: requests (started_at, request_id); definition parts (item_id, path); source nodes (item_id, parent_id, source_type, source_id), null parent first; ACL entries (scope_type, scope_id, principal_type, principal_id, role, inheritance_path); transitions (observed_at, state); redactions/unavailable fields (json_path, marker_type, reason_code); reviews (reviewed_at, reviewer_id). The offline validator parses calendar-valid timestamps, checks stable ordering and verifies every nested live-record manifest hash and window id against the shared baseline binding. Every top-level key from REQ-008 is required. Each contributing live record binds window_id and window_manifest_sha256. Public scalar strings are short and restricted to a conservative syntax, numeric values are bounded integers, and excluded values must use typed markers. These constraints do not prove content safety or that a field was approved; independent redaction/content review remains required. Top-level hashes contains detached records for included artifacts; the baseline own digest must remain in a separate detached hash record.",
